    "created_at": "2023-03-23T11:17:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-23T11:17:25Z",
    "body": "> ```toml\r\n> [rlang] \r\n> detect_files = [] \r\n> ```\r\n\r\nThat would disable the module in project folders with `.R`/`.Rmd`/etc. files though, right?\r\n\r\nI came here because I was looking for a solution to this, and was wondering if the `when` config option for custom modules could maybe be supported for other modules as well?\r\nE.g. `when = ''' test \"$HOME\" != \"$PWD\" '''`\r\n\r\nBut then again, if _any of_ `when`, `detect_files` and `detect_folders` are sufficient to trigger the module, then that's likely not sufficient either :/\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
